{"id":"libnah","name":"Libnah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:libnah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Libnah","text":"Transparency; whiteness. (1.) One of the stations of the Israelites in the wilderness (Num. 33:20, 21). (2.) One of the royal cities of the Canaanites taken by Joshua (Josh. 10:29-32; 12:15). It became one of the Levitical towns in the tribe of Judah (21:13), and was strongly fortified. Sennacherib laid siege to it (2 Kings 19:8; Isa. 37:8). It was the native place of Hamutal, the queen of Josiah (2 Kings 23:31). It stood near Lachish, and has been identified with the modern Arak el-Menshiyeh."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3841","lemma":"לִבְנָה","xlit":"Libnâh","gloss":"Libnah, a place in the Desert and one in Palestine","kjv":"Libnah","count":10,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H804","lemma":"אַשּׁוּר","xlit":"ʼAshshûwr","gloss":"Ashshur, the second son of Shem","kjv":"Asshur, Assur, Assyria, Assyrians. See H838","count":9,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H2396","lemma":"חִזְקִיָּה","xlit":"Chizqîyâh","gloss":"Chizkijah, a king of Judah, also the name of two other I","kjv":"Hezekiah, Hizkiah, Hizkijah","count":5,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H3923","lemma":"לָכִישׁ","xlit":"Lâkîysh","gloss":"Lakish, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Lachish","count":4,"share":0.1},{"strong":"H3898","lemma":"לָחַם","xlit":"lâcham","gloss":"to feed on","kjv":"devour, eat, ever, fight","count":5,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H4397","lemma":"מֲלְאָךְ","xlit":"mălʼâk","gloss":"a messenger","kjv":"ambassador, angel, king, messenger","count":4,"share":0.1}],"verses":["Num.33.20","Josh.10.29","Josh.10.31","Josh.10.32","Josh.10.39","Josh.12.15","Josh.21.13","2Kgs.19.8","1Chr.6.57","Isa.37.8","Josh.10.30","2Kgs.19.35","Isa.37.9","Isa.37.10","Isa.37.11","Isa.37.12","Isa.37.13","Isa.37.14","Isa.37.15","Isa.37.16","Isa.37.17","Isa.37.18","Isa.37.19","Isa.37.20","Isa.37.21","Isa.37.22","Isa.37.23","Isa.37.24","Isa.37.25","Isa.37.26","Isa.37.27","Isa.37.28","Isa.37.29",